# Few-Shot RAG Resume Intelligence — Implementation Plan

## Background & Context

We have two powerful assets to build from:

1. **37 verified Day 1 consulting resumes** from IIT Bombay seniors who secured internships at McKinsey, Bain, BCG, LEK, PwC US Advisory, Accenture, NRI, and HUL — stored in `data/resumes/consult/`.
2. **"Resume Making Session" best practices guide** (54 pages) from seniors — stored in `data/resumes/Resume Making Session.pdf`.

The best practices guide encodes explicit structural rules that we must bake into the AI's critique engine as hard constraints:

| Rule | Source (Page) |
|------|------|
| Each bullet: **Impact Word → What? → Effect → How?** | p9 |
| Avoid 2-line sub-points; every sub-point should complete the line | p8 |
| Organize sub-points: sequentially, most impactful first | p8 |
| Quantify with numbers/percentages everywhere possible | p11, p20, p22 |
| Bold only tool/library/algorithm names, not entire phrases | p12 |
| No full stops at end of sentences | p11 |
| Don't repeat action verbs across bullets | p9 |
| POR flow: Team & budget size → Your role → New initiatives → Effect of work | p26 |
| Professional Experience: What → Responsibilities → How → Impact → Awards | p22 |
| Projects: Problem statement → Methodology → Results (with metrics) | p24, p39 |
| Use STAR framework (Situation, Task, Action, Result) | p40 |
| Eye-tracking: recruiter spends ~7 seconds; most recent experience gets most attention | p47 |
| Interpersonal skills >>> Technical skills for non-core roles | p48 |
| "Weave your story" — resume should have a coherent narrative thread | p52 |

**Critical Design Constraint:** The system must **never** copy or suggest using specific facts, projects, or achievements from the golden resumes. It extracts only the **structural framing patterns** — action verbs, metric placement, impact quantification style, and sentence architecture — and uses those as benchmarks for critique.

